    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesn't feel temporary. it feels permanent. like the fog has finally settled and there is nothing left to see. the more i look at the path behind me, the more it just looks like a series of mistakes and exhaustion. standing here at the edge... it's the first time in a long time that things have actually felt quiet. do you get that? that sense that the stillness at the edge is more real than the struggle to keep walking?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
